  "description": "This apple crumble is enhanced with juicy stone fruit and honey for a dessert that’s perfect for Rosh Hashanah or any September gathering.",
  "notes": "Optional substitutions: almonds → walnuts\n\nNotes: We recommend using a mix of firm, tart apples like Fuji and Jonagold, as well as softer Golden Delicious.\nYou can use packaged oat flour, but I prefer the medium-grind texture that the extra step of grinding whole oats offers.\n\nMake-ahead and storage: The finished crumble can be refrigerated in an airtight container for up to 5 days.",
